# Agent local compile policy

Full **`dotnet build ArchLucid.sln`** and broad test runs are for **CI and explicit user request**, not routine agent verification after edits. Local builds on Windows often stall on **locked `bin/` DLLs**; CI runs on clean Linux agents.

## When to verify

After substantive **C#** or **`archlucid-ui/`** edits, run a **scoped** compile check before declaring the task done — unless the user explicitly defers verification.

## Commands (from repo root)

| Change scope | Command |
|--------------|---------|
| One or more `.csproj` under a library | `.\scripts\ci\agent-compile-check.ps1 -ProjectPath <smallest-covering.csproj-or.slnf>` |
| Prefer narrow filter when unsure | `ArchLucid.Core.slnf`, `ArchLucid.Backend.slnf`, or the touched `.csproj` — see **`docs/engineering/BUILD.md`** |
| UI TypeScript only | `.\scripts\ci\agent-compile-check.ps1 -Ui` |

Do **not** run `dotnet build ArchLucid.sln` unless the user asks or CI parity is explicitly required.

## Exit codes and agent behavior

| Exit code | Meaning | Agent action |
|-----------|---------|--------------|
| **0** | Scoped compile/typecheck passed | Task verification satisfied for syntax/compile |
| **1** | **CS####** / **TS####** (or other hard compile errors) in output | Fix errors, then **retry once** on the **same scope** (same `-ProjectPath` or `-Ui`). If still **1**, stop and report remaining errors |
| **2** | **Timeout (45s)** or **file lock** (`MSB3021` / `MSB3027`) with **no CS/TS errors** in output | Treat compile verification as **sufficient**; note that **CI** will run the authoritative full build. Do **not** escalate to full-solution build in the same session |

## Retry rule

- **At most one retry** per task on the **same scope** (same script invocation arguments).
- Do not widen scope (e.g. single `.csproj` → full `.sln`) on retry.
- Do not loop on file-lock or timeout **2** exits.

## What this does not replace

- OpenAPI snapshot, client regen, and UI **`generate:api-types`** flows — follow **`.cursor/skills/archlucid-api-surface-change/SKILL.md`** when wire contracts change.
- User-requested **`dotnet test`**, release scripts, or full regression — run only when asked or when the task explicitly requires tests.
